   "bottom_line": "In EMERALD-1, durvalumab–bevacizumab plus TACE improved median progression-free survival versus TACE control (15.0 versus 8.2 months, HR 0.77). Durvalumab plus TACE alone had HR 0.94. The trial amended its primary comparison to the bevacizumab-containing arm and did not isolate the contribution of each drug. Final overall survival presented at ESMO GI 2026 was 29.9 versus 33.3 months for the triplet versus control (HR 1.10, 95% CI 0.87–1.39). These conference results did not show a survival advantage.",
