    "n": "IMbrave050 randomised 668 of 914 screened patients after curative-intent resection (585, 88%) or ablation (83, 12%) for HCC at high risk of recurrence. Patients received atezolizumab–bevacizumab for up to 12 months or active surveillance. Overall 545/668 (82%) were Asian, 71% enrolled in Asia-Pacific excluding Japan and 416/668 (62%) had HBV.",
    "bottom_line": "At the prespecified interim analysis, adjuvant atezolizumab–bevacizumab improved recurrence-free survival versus surveillance (HR 0.72, adjusted 95% CI 0.53–0.98, P = 0.012). The median was not estimable in either arm. The updated analysis did not sustain the benefit. Grade 3–4 events of any cause occurred in 136/332 (41%) with treatment versus 44/330 (13%) with surveillance. Treatment-related grade 3–4 events occurred in 35% and two treatment-related deaths were reported. Crossover at recurrence complicates overall survival interpretation.",
