   "bottom_line": "Establishes a complete US reference for HCC, from at-risk populations and surveillance intervals through diagnosis, expanded transplant and downstaging criteria, TACE and Y-90 suitability, and first- and second-line systemic therapy, with tables a tumour board can use directly. It does not establish its recommendations at the strength their labels imply: there was no mandatory systematic review, no GRADE and no meta-analysis, Strong Recommendations are permitted on expert opinion, and two of its positions, adjuvant immunotherapy and the prohibition on TACE plus systemic therapy, have since been reversed or overtaken. Use the tables; check the statements against the 2025 critical update and the 2026 BCLC update before acting on them.",
   "funding": "Funding for the development of this Practice Guidance was provided by the AASLD. Conflicts are declared at length: the first author consults for Genentech, AstraZeneca, Eisai, Bayer, Boston Scientific, Exelixis, FujiFilm Medical Sciences, Exact Sciences, Glycotest and Universal Diagnostics; the second consults for and has received grants from Eisai, Bayer and Ipsen and consults for eleven further companies; other authors report institutional grants from Merck, Genentech, Incyte, Bristol-Myers Squibb and Gilead, stock in a pharmaceutical company, and speakers' bureau roles, while the remaining authors report none"
