    "bottom_line": "A 29-patient single-arm study showing that an ablative segmental Y-90 dose produces complete response in 83 percent of target lesions initially and sustained complete response in 90 percent, with complete necrosis of all eight target lesions that reached explant. It is a response study with no comparator, one unmasked in-house reader, 24 months of follow-up and 44 percent of patients censored by transplant or loss, so it does not show that radiation segmentectomy matches ablation for recurrence or survival.",
