    "bottom_line": "Baveno VII defines clinically significant portal hypertension (CSPH) by an HVPG of at least 10 mmHg in viral- and alcohol-related cirrhosis. In compensated advanced chronic liver disease, liver stiffness at most 15 kPa with platelets at least 150 × 10⁹/L rules out CSPH. Stiffness at least 25 kPa rules it in for viral- or alcohol-related disease and non-obese NASH. ANTICIPATE estimates intermediate risk in those groups. CSPH increases risk after HCC resection, but the consensus gives no universal threshold for declining surgery.",
    "funding": "The participants reported no conflicts related to the Baveno VII manuscript. EASL, AASLD, eight national groups and three European research consortia supported the workshop with unrestricted grants. Two authors separately declared industry relationships, and foundation support was also reported."
