    "bottom_line": "Establishes a graded, multidisciplinary framework for where external beam radiotherapy fits in HCC and intrahepatic cholangiocarcinoma, with dose, fractionation and organ-at-risk tables a radiation oncologist can work from, and makes EBRT a named first-line option for liver-confined HCC when curative treatment is not available. It does not establish that EBRT is equivalent or preferable to ablation, embolisation or surgery, because no randomised comparison with any of them existed at the February 2020 search cut-off and the grading scheme permits a Strong recommendation to rest on expert opinion. Read it as radiation oncology's consensus on how to deliver EBRT well, not as evidence on whether to choose it.",
